  "id": "best-interests-of-the-child",
  "term": "best interests of the child",
  "definition": "The best interests of the child is a legal and ethical principle in custody decisions that requires judges to put the child’s welfare first and choose the outcome most beneficial to the child. In practice, this means focusing on the child’s needs, including emotional and psychological well-being, rather than treating parental claims alone as decisive.",
